  - q: 'A research team tests 150 ideas a year. About 10 are real. Tests catch 80% of real signals and wrongly pass 5% of useless ones. Roughly what share of the signals that pass are real?'
    opts: ['About half', 'About 95%', 'About 80%']
    right: 0
    why: 'Real finds: \(10 \times 0.8 = 8\). False finds: \(140 \times 0.05 = 7\). So \(8\) of the \(15\) passes are real, just over half. Because most ideas are useless, even a strict-sounding test lets through nearly as much noise as signal.'
